{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And now restore the man's wife, etc.</b> The saying <b>for he is a prophet</b> means that the man whose wife this is — he is a prophet, for He still did not know explicitly that she was Abraham's wife, since in their words the husband was not mentioned, as we wrote above. And in saying ״he is a prophet,״ it is known that he is Abraham, for there was no prophet other than him in those days." "<b>Further,</b> it intends <b>for he is a prophet</b> — and he knows that even though she was hidden away [with you], she was not defiled." "<b>Further,</b> it intends along this line: <b>for he is a prophet</b> — and by this [virtue] he will pray on your behalf and his prayer will avail, which is what He means by <b>and live.</b>"], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:28.978702225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}